<section>
  <grid spacing="medium">
    <grid-item colspan="34" vertical-align="center">
      <labels><label variant="outline">Log entry 01</label></labels>
      <h2>The log begins hot and dense</h2>
      <p>Open the log with the observable universe in an extremely hot, dense early state. As space expanded, the universe cooled. Measurements place this history at about <b>13.8 billion years</b>.</p>
      <p>This is not a bomb’s launch time in a pre-existing void. The model describes the universe changing with time, not matter flying into an outer sea.</p>
      <p font-size="sm">Source: <a href="https://science.nasa.gov/universe/overview/">NASA · Universe Overview</a></p>
    </grid-item>
    <grid-item colspan="26" padding="0">
      <ai-image background="true" image-style="celestial-copperplate" aspect-ratio="portrait" prompt="Digitally illustrated copperplate celestial engraving of the early cosmos as a uniformly dense luminous field extending beyond the frame, nested ivory coordinate meshes, oxidized-brass scientific instrument arcs, cyan radiation traces diffused everywhere with one restrained coral highlight, no central point, no outward blast, no text or lettering"></ai-image>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>